      "writtenOn": "2021-10-12T16:43:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It could be useful to distinguish `Dead` from `Failed`, and to know the payload state even after the VM died. I think it would be simpler and more useful to just include both vm_state and payload_state in the output, and then you can just use their `Debug` implementations rather than this match expression. I.e. something like:\n\n```\nformat!(\"{:?} (payload {:?})\", instance.vm_state.lock().unwrap(), instance.payload_state())\n```\n\nAnd then the separate function is not really needed, it can just be inline in `dump`.",
